// 1000 Cuts (25 Oct 2026): a dated chronology of every event that lowered the Williams family's standing in law, from the peak to
// the 1988 eviction and demolition, with each cut's evidence page, its blow, and its dependencies (the pyramid). Data: cedwyn
// catalogue database (layer 'thousand-cuts'); source JSON work/thousand-cuts/cuts.json. Our reading, not a finding of any court. — Sion's Tab agent
export const THOUSAND_CUTS_PAGES = {"/timeline/thousand-cuts/": {"title": "1000 Cuts: how the Williams family's standing in law was cut down (1916–1988)", "html": "<style>.tc{--tc-line:rgba(127,127,127,.35);--tc-soft:rgba(127,127,127,.08);--tc-acc:#b5651d;--tc-rec:#2e7d32;--tc-tes:#6a1b9a;--tc-inf:#1565c0;--tc-nyc:#8d6e00;max-width:46rem;margin:0 auto;line-height:1.55;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n.tc *{box-sizing:border-box}.tc h2{margin:1.6em 0 .4em;font-size:1.3em;border-bottom:1px solid var(--tc-line);padding-bottom:.2em}.tc h3{margin:1.2em 0 .3em;font-size:1.08em}\n.tc .lede{font-size:1.05em}.tc .muted{opacity:.75;font-size:.92em}\n.tc .pyr{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:3px;margin:1em 0 .5em}.tc .pyr a{display:block;text-align:center;font-size:.8em;padding:4px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:var(--tc-soft);border:1px solid var(--tc-line);color:inherit;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;max-width:100%}\n.tc .pyr a.apex{background:rgba(181,101,29,.18);border-color:var(--tc-acc)}\n.tc .lyr{margin:1.4em 0 .2em;padding:.5em .7em;border-left:4px solid var(--tc-acc);background:var(--tc-soft);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0}\n.tc .lyr b{display:block}.tc .mini{display:flex;flex-direction:column-reverse;align-items:center;gap:2px;float:right;margin:2px 0 4px 10px}\n.tc .mini i{display:block;height:5px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--tc-line)}.tc .mini i.on{background:var(--tc-acc)}\n.tc .cut{border:1px solid var(--tc-line);border-radius:8px;padding:.6em .75em;margin:.6em 0;scroll-margin-top:90px}\n.tc .cut.ctx{border-style:dashed;opacity:.9}.tc .cut .hd{display:flex;gap:.5em;align-items:baseline;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.tc .cid{font-weight:700;font-family:ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-size:.9em}.tc .dt{font-weight:600}\n.tc .ev{margin:.3em 0}.tc .blow{margin:.35em 0;padding:.35em .55em;background:var(--tc-soft);border-radius:6px}\n.tc .blow b{color:var(--tc-acc)}.tc .refs a,.tc .deps a{display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:1px 7px;border:1px solid var(--tc-line);border-radius:10px;font-size:.82em;text-decoration:none}\n.tc .deps{font-size:.88em;margin-top:.3em}.tc .lab{font-size:.75em;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid currentColor;white-space:nowrap}\n.tc .l-rec{color:var(--tc-rec)}.tc .l-tes{color:var(--tc-tes)}.tc .l-inf{color:var(--tc-inf)}.tc .l-nyc{color:var(--tc-nyc)}\n.tc .spine{list-style:none;padding:0;margin:.5em 0}.tc .spine li{padding:.2em 0 .2em .9em;border-left:2px solid var(--tc-acc);margin-left:.3em;font-size:.92em}\n.tc .reading{border:2px solid var(--tc-acc);border-radius:8px;padding:.6em .8em}.tc ul.tight{padding-left:1.2em}.tc ul.tight li{margin:.25em 0}\n@media (max-width:420px){.tc{font-size:15px}.tc .pyr a{font-size:.74em}}</style><div class=\"tc\" id=\"tc-top\">\n<p class=\"lede\">How the Williams family&#x27;s standing in law was cut down, from the peak to the fall. Each cut below is a dated event that lowered the Williams family's standing in the eyes of the law. Each one links to its evidence page and shows what it depended on and what it made possible. Read from the bottom layer up: by the top, the eviction and demolition of 1988 rest on everything beneath them.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Record = read in a court judgment, registry, archive, legislation or contemporaneous press. Family testimony = the family&#x27;s own account. Our reading = interpretation. Not yet confirmed = no source located yet. The dependency links are our reading of how the record fits together. This page is our case and interpretation. It is not a finding of any court.</p>\n<h2>The pyramid at a glance</h2><div class=\"pyr\" aria-label=\"Pyramid of cuts, apex at the top\">\n<a href=\"#layer-9\" style=\"width:34%\" class=\"apex\">9. 1988: the fall (8)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-8\" style=\"width:41%\" class=\"\">8. 1984–87: the courts (4)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-7\" style=\"width:48%\" class=\"\">7. 1982–83: registration and a death (5)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-6\" style=\"width:55%\" class=\"\">6. 1975: the house moves within BP (2)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-5\" style=\"width:62%\" class=\"\">5. 1974: the revival and the letters (4)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-4\" style=\"width:69%\" class=\"\">4. A new owner (1966–1972) (4)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-3\" style=\"width:76%\" class=\"\">3. Orders and offers (1955–1965) (5)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-2\" style=\"width:83%\" class=\"\">2. Tenancy, arrears and lost papers (1945–1954) (5)</a>\n<a href=\"#layer-1\" style=\"width:90%\" class=\"\">1. The paper frame (1916–1940) (3)</a>\n<a href=\"#peak\" style=\"width:100%\">The peak: the base everything was cut from (7)</a></div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Tap a layer to jump to it. The story below runs from the base upwards.</p>\n<h2 id=\"peak\">The peak</h2><p>The base of the pyramid: the family at its height on Parcel A, the house parcel, and the manorial farmhouse. Some of this is on record, and some is family testimony or not yet confirmed; each item is labelled.</p>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p1\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P1</span><span class=\"dt\">1870s–1916</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names him; the 1904 Bute rent audit lists him &quot;of Llandough Farm&quot;.</div><div class=\"blow\">The family&#x27;s long occupation is on record. The same records describe it as a tenancy from Bute, which is the frame the law later used.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0227-cardiff-times-1904-john-williams-tenancy-since-1855/\">EV-0227</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Cut into by: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01</a> <a href=\"#c06\" title=\"c.1950–52 · Family title papers removed from the farmhouse blanket box.\">C06</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p2\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P2</span><span class=\"dt\">May 1897</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Marconi&#x27;s wireless tests at Lavernock and Flat Holm, close by. Family tradition holds that he stayed at the farm.</div><div class=\"blow\">The 1897 press and Kemp&#x27;s diary extracts record the tests but do not name Great House Farm. The stay would be confirmed by the full Kemp diary (Bodleian MS. Marconi 89) or a letter placing the team at the farm.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0011-marconi-lavernock-wireless-cutting-1897/\">EV-0011</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0248-marconi-in-wales-may-1897-contemporary-press/\">EV-0248</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0256-kemp-diary-lavernock-1897-bodleian-ms-marconi-89/\">EV-0256</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p3\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P3</span><span class=\"dt\">1890s (year not yet found)</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed</span></div><div class=\"ev\">&quot;Peerless&quot; Jim Driscoll&#x27;s first fight in the farm barn.</div><div class=\"blow\">A secondary local-history summary places the fight in the barn; the year and the National Monuments Record citation have not yet been located.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p4\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P4</span><span class=\"dt\">1891 to 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Tree planting on Parcel A, the house parcel, as an act of ownership, with the town as witness; the family&#x27;s acts of occupation.</div><div class=\"blow\">Testimony and an undated photograph. Dated photographs, aerial images or survey sheets would confirm the planting and its extent.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0009-family-tree-planting-parcel-a/\">EV-0009</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0199-photograph-tree-planting-at-great-house-farm-date/\">EV-0199</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p5\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P5</span><span class=\"dt\">1928</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Last rent for the house parcel paid in 1928, when the quarry machinery left; no rent for the house parcel after that.</div><div class=\"blow\">Mary (Nancy) Williams&#x27;s recollection; the receipt is not located. Cuts against: the Court of Appeal recorded rent arrears in the mid-1930s and late 1940s and a last payment, under a judgment for arrears, in 1953.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p6\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P6</span><span class=\"dt\">1928 to 1949</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">No one takes issue with the stopped rent for about twenty years, until the 1949 surrender and re-grant.</div><div class=\"blow\">Our reading of the family account. The judgment instead records arrears &quot;in the mid-1930s and in the late 1940s&quot; as the reason for the 1949 arrangement.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"p7\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">P7</span><span class=\"dt\">1939</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The 1939 Western Ground Rents agreement plan shows the fields (Parcel B) only, highlighted; the house parcel is not shown on it.</div><div class=\"blow\">Supports the family&#x27;s reading that the house parcel stood apart from the let fields. Page 1 of the agreement is not yet held.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0023-1939-wgr-john-williams-tenancy-plan/\">EV-0023</a></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"cuts\">The cuts</h2><p>39 cuts and 1 background step, from 1916 to 7 December 1988, in 9 layers.</p>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-1\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 1 of 9: The paper frame (1916–1940)</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 0 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c01\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C01</span><span class=\"dt\">Feb 1916</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The first paper that names the family as tenants. Every later court began from it: the Court of Appeal opens with Bute letting &quot;the whole of the farm&quot; to John Williams.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0014-bute-tenancy-john-williams-1916/\">EV-0014</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#p1\" title=\"1870s–1916 · John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names h\">P1</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance \">C02</a> <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c02\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C02</span><span class=\"dt\">23–25 Dec 1938</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later becomes the root of title.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The landlord the family knew is replaced by a company holding a paper title. From here a written chain runs to BP; the family hold no paper of their own in it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0019-bute-wgr-conveyance-plan-1938/\">EV-0019</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0022-press-1938-bute-wgr-sale-completion/\">EV-0022</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0216-1965-contract-condition-f-conveyance-25-december-1938/\">EV-0216</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04</a> <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c03\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C03</span><span class=\"dt\">1 Jul 1940</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (the Act, as applied in the 1987 judgment)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession must be &quot;adverse&quot;; s.13 a formal entry alone keeps nothing alive).</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> It set the 12-year test the family would be judged by. Under it, a tenancy, a rent payment, a court action or a licence stops or restarts the clock, so each later step against the family was measured against this Act.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: the law of the day (no earlier cut)<br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a> <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07</a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under\">C18</a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforce\">C19</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-2\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 2 of 9: Tenancy, arrears and lost papers (1945–1954)</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 1 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c04\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C04</span><span class=\"dt\">mid-1930s and late 1940s</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> In the law&#x27;s eyes the stopped rent became arrears owed by a tenant, not the end of a tenancy. This is the opposite of the family&#x27;s 1928 account, and it is the version the court accepted.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0016-1928-last-rent-receipt-quarrying/\">EV-0016</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01</a> <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance \">C02</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c05\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C05</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1949</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (the grant); our reading (its purpose)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Frederick Buckler. It is never put in writing.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> Occupation passed from the Williams line to a yearly tenant, so the family&#x27;s presence was recast as permission. On our reading this is the first deliberate step to make the occupancy of Parcel A look permissive.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0025-frederick-buckler-unwritten-tenancy-1949/\">EV-0025</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04</a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession mu\">C03</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07</a> <a href=\"#c08\" title=\"1954 · A further attempt to treat Frederick Buckler as a tenant.\">C08</a> <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c06\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C06</span><span class=\"dt\">c.1950–52</span><span class=\"lab l-tes\">Family testimony</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Family title papers removed from the farmhouse blanket box.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The family lost the documents they would later need to prove a title of their own. No court ever saw them.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0026-family-title-papers-removed-blanket-box/\">EV-0026</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#p1\" title=\"1870s–1916 · John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names h\">P1</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c07\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C07</span><span class=\"dt\">1953</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> A payment under a judgment acknowledged the landlord&#x27;s title, so no 12-year clock could run before it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession mu\">C03</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c08\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C08</span><span class=\"dt\">1954</span><span class=\"lab l-nyc\">Not yet confirmed (source pending)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">A further attempt to treat Frederick Buckler as a tenant.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> Another step putting the family&#x27;s occupation on a tenancy footing.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0031-1954-buckler-tenancy-attempt/\">EV-0031</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-3\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 3 of 9: Orders and offers (1955–1965)</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 2 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c09\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C09</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The family were now occupiers with no tenancy. The Court of Appeal later held that Frederick and Mary were in adverse possession of the house and garden from this date, so the clock did start.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a> <a href=\"#c07\" title=\"1953 · Frederick Buckler&#x27;s last rent payment, made under a county-court judgment for arrears.\">C07</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c10\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C10</span><span class=\"dt\">1955 and 4 Jul 1955</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (the judgment); the order itself is not yet located</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July 1955: all the farm is taken except the farmhouse and garden.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The fields were lost in one summary step. The house survived only because Mary had just had a leg amputated and refused to leave. From then on the family held the house alone, against a court order.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0032-1955-order-14-possession-order/\">EV-0032</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0034-writ-possession-execution-return-1955/\">EV-0034</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09</a> <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance \">C02</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c11\" title=\"1958 · Leckwith Common inquiry and Glamorgan County Council acquisitions near the farm; Mary&#x27;s &quot;Crichel Down&quot; objection \">C11</a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing\">C12</a> <a href=\"#c16\" title=\"16 Jun 1970 · Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.\">C16</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c11\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C11</span><span class=\"dt\">1958</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press); our reading (its effect)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Leckwith Common inquiry and Glamorgan County Council acquisitions near the farm; Mary&#x27;s &quot;Crichel Down&quot; objection goes no further, and no petition is presented in Parliament.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The land around the house passed into public schemes while her objection had no legal effect. Our reading: it showed the family&#x27;s word carried no weight with public bodies.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0035-western-mail-1958-leckwith-common-hearing/\">EV-0035</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0036-western-mail-1958-gcc-acquisition-notice/\">EV-0036</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0037-western-mail-1958-crichel-down/\">EV-0037</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0038-hansard-1958-leckwith-common-no-petition/\">EV-0038</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c12\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C12</span><span class=\"dt\">1959 and Mar 1965</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing is offered and refused.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The offers built a paper record of the family as would-be tenants. In 1986 the trial judge used the March 1965 offer to find that Frederick had no intention to possess as owner.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0039-wgr-tenancy-offers-1959-1965/\">EV-0039</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c13\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C13</span><span class=\"dt\">11 Dec 1962</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profits; a suspended committal order against Frederick Buckler follows in June 1963.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The decisive cut of the 1960s. Because it came before 12 years had run, the Court of Appeal held the owner&#x27;s title was never extinguished. The order then lay unused for 12 years and was revived in 1974.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0030-cardiff-county-court-registers-aca/\">EV-0030</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09</a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession mu\">C03</a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing\">C12</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c14\" title=\"1965–67 · Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.\">C14</a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforce\">C19</a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-4\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 4 of 9: A new owner (1966–1972)</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 3 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c14\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C14</span><span class=\"dt\">1965–67</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The trial judge held that while he lived only his intention counted, so Mary&#x27;s own clear intention to own was given no effect before his death.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c15\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C15</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Dec 1969</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> A national institution with full legal resources took over the paper title and, as successor, the benefit of the 1962 order.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0043-wgr-bp-pension-trust-conveyance/\">EV-0043</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance \">C02</a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c17\" title=\"1972 · Outline planning permission for about 13 houses, with an ownership certificate.\">C17</a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under\">C18</a> <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforce\">C19</a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and se\">C22</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c16\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C16</span><span class=\"dt\">16 Jun 1970</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (registration); our reading (its effect) — weakened</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> In the family&#x27;s frame, one of three &quot;synthetic&quot; versions of Parcel A made without the occupier. Cuts against: the certified map shows a small roadside wedge, so this reading is weak on the map read so far.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0263-commons-registration-1965-publicity-glamorgan-notices-vg41/\">EV-0263</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c28\" title=\"26 Jul 1983 (in force 1 Sep 1983) · The Commons Registration (Glamorgan) Act 1983 validates the Glamorgan common-land re\">C28</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c17\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C17</span><span class=\"dt\">1972</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (planning register)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Outline planning permission for about 13 houses, with an ownership certificate.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The owner certified ownership to the planning authority and planned houses on the site. On paper the land was already a development site with the family inside it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0046-1972-outline-planning-permission-ownership-certificate/\">EV-0046</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-5\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 5 of 9: 1974: the revival and the letters</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 4 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c18\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C18</span><span class=\"dt\">3 Jul 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under the 1939 Act. The action is adjourned part-heard and &quot;has never been finally heard&quot;.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> Her plea of ownership was never decided. It still sits undecided on the court file, so it was never won and never lost.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0049-mary-williams-plea-ownership-pleadings/\">EV-0049</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession mu\">C03</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c19\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C19</span><span class=\"dt\">17–19 Sep 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from 31 Oct 1974. She appeals, saying she had too little notice to be heard.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> A 12-year-old order was revived about 12 weeks before the 12-year period from it ran out (11 Dec 1974), without her being heard.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0041-cardiff-county-court-possession-order-1962/\">EV-0041</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a> <a href=\"#c03\" title=\"1 Jul 1940 · The Limitation Act 1939 comes into force: 12 years of adverse possession bars the owner (s.10 possession mu\">C03</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c20\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C20</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Oct 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for life: &quot;no proceedings will be commenced until you personally no longer live there&quot;.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The cut the courts rested on. Written without her agreement, the letters made her possession &quot;by the licence of BP Properties&quot;, so it was no longer adverse. Her occupation was turned into permission by letter.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0048-telegraph-open-day-ancient-house/\">EV-0048</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforce\">C19</a> <a href=\"#c18\" title=\"3 Jul 1974 · BP Pension Trust&#x27;s new possession action: Mary pleads that BP&#x27;s claim is barred by adverse possession under\">C18</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not r\">C21</a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and se\">C22</a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a> <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26</a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29</a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c21\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C21</span><span class=\"dt\">Nov–Dec 1974</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject the letters.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The Court of Appeal held that &quot;she did not, however, do that&quot; (reject the letters). Her silence was read as accepting the permission rather than claiming ownership.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0050-1974-bp-licence-letters/\">EV-0050</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-6\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 6 of 9: 1975: the house moves within BP</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 5 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c22\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C22</span><span class=\"dt\">23 May 1975</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and sewer rights &quot;to serve any development&quot;.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The house passed to the company that wrote the licence letter, with development rights built into the deed.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0052-bp-pension-trust-bp-properties-conveyance/\">EV-0052</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a> <a href=\"#c15\" title=\"31 Dec 1969 · Western Ground Rents sells the farm, including the farmhouse, to BP Pension Trust.\">C15</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required \">C24</a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c23\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C23</span><span class=\"dt\">1 Dec 1975</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> This brought in the machinery that would turn BP&#x27;s paper title into a title guaranteed by the state.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0265-hmlr-registration-background-compulsory-1975-r29-certificate/\">EV-0265</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: the law of the day (no earlier cut)<br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required \">C24</a> <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-7\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 7 of 9: 1982–83: registration and a death</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 6 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut ctx\" id=\"c24\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C24</span><span class=\"dt\">19 and 30 Nov 1982</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (context)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required within two months.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>Why it matters:</b> Background only. It left the farmhouse as the only unregistered piece of the BP farm.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0059-wa231076-form-a13-first-registration/\">EV-0059</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and se\">C22</a> <a href=\"#c23\" title=\"1 Dec 1975 · The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.\">C23</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a> <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pendi\">C31</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c25\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C25</span><span class=\"dt\">23 Feb 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (application, date); our reading (what had to be sworn)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has to swear BP is in possession. This was BP&#x27;s only voluntary filing.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The family home was put on the state register in BP&#x27;s name, dated as of a day she lived there. BP&#x27;s &quot;possession&quot; could only be her occupation as its licensee under the 1974 letters.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0066-hmlr-wa240304-item-10-register-1983/\">EV-0066</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0063-hmlr-wa240304-item-11-form-1c/\">EV-0063</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0065-wa240304-farmhouse-first-registration-file/\">EV-0065</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and se\">C22</a> <a href=\"#c23\" title=\"1 Dec 1975 · The Vale of Glamorgan becomes a compulsory registration area.\">C23</a> <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required \">C24</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form \">C27</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c26\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C26</span><span class=\"dt\">26 Mar 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (month); family record (day); testimony (illness)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> BP&#x27;s own undertaking (&quot;until you personally no longer live there&quot;) fell away. In BP&#x27;s own words in 1988, her death was when &quot;it became clear her son was not going to leave&quot;.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0067-mary-doreen-williams-death-index/\">EV-0067</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form \">C27</a> <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c27\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C27</span><span class=\"dt\">8 Apr – 12 May 1983</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (letters exist); our reading (their effect)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form D23), correspondence of 12 Apr and letters of 12 May 1983.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The title was completed after she died, but it speaks from a date when she was alive. What the letters told the Registry about who lived there is not yet known; the Registry&#x27;s copy file (due 28 Oct 2026) would confirm it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0069-hmlr-wa240304-item-7-d23-1983/\">EV-0069</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0070-hmlr-wa240304-item-4-correspondence-1983/\">EV-0070</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0071-wa231076-1983-84-registration-activity/\">EV-0071</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a> <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pendi\">C31</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c28\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C28</span><span class=\"dt\">26 Jul 1983 (in force 1 Sep 1983)</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (the Act); our reading — no direct effect found</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The Commons Registration (Glamorgan) Act 1983 validates the Glamorgan common-land registers.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> Parliament confirmed the registers made without the family. Cuts against: the Act covers common land only, not village greens, so on our reading it did not touch VG41 or the farmhouse directly.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0232-commons-registration-glamorgan-act-1983/\">EV-0232</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0044-vg41-village-green-registration-1970/\">EV-0044</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c16\" title=\"16 Jun 1970 · Village green VG41 registered by Glamorgan County Council.\">C16</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-8\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 8 of 9: 1984–87: the courts</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 7 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c29\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C29</span><span class=\"dt\">May 1984</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The family were now defending, not claiming. The son was sued as an occupier with no licence, and his own 12-year period had barely begun.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0073-family-solicitors-litigation-file-1984-87/\">EV-0073</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26</a> <a href=\"#c22\" title=\"23 May 1975 · BP Pension Trust conveys the farmhouse plot and other land to BP Properties, reserving 80-year road and se\">C22</a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c30\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C30</span><span class=\"dt\">10–24 Jul 1986</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The first decision on the merits. It held Frederick&#x27;s possession was not adverse and the letters made Mary a licensee, so the defence under the 1939 and 1980 Acts failed.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0074-high-court-trial-judgment-1986/\">EV-0074</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0075-south-wales-echo-1986-high-court-judgment/\">EV-0075</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29</a> <a href=\"#c14\" title=\"1965–67 · Frederick Buckler dies. Mary stays in the house.\">C14</a> <a href=\"#c12\" title=\"1959 and Mar 1965 · Western Ground Rents offers Mary a tenancy of the house and garden; she refuses. Alternative housing\">C12</a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a> <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not r\">C21</a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pendi\">C31</a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c31\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C31</span><span class=\"dt\">2 Feb 1987</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (application); our reading (class of title)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pending.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The house disappeared into BP&#x27;s larger title before the appeal was heard. Our reading: if the 1983 title had been possessory, upgrading it while an adverse claim was open was barred from 1 Jan 1987. This is not yet confirmed.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0078-1987-title-amalgamation-application-plan/\">EV-0078</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c27\" title=\"8 Apr – 12 May 1983 · The Registry examines the farmhouse application after her death: Linklaters letter of 8 Apr (form \">C27</a> <a href=\"#c24\" title=\"19 and 30 Nov 1982 · The fields (Parcel B) pass between BP companies and are registered (WA231076), as the law required \">C24</a> <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c32\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C32</span><span class=\"dt\">31 Jul 1987</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; leave to appeal to the House of Lords refused.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The licence-by-letter reasoning became binding law, and ownership itself was never decided. The court accepted that Frederick and Mary were in adverse possession from 1955, but held that the 1962 order and the 1974 letters defeated it.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0080-bp-properties-v-buckler-judgment/\">EV-0080</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a> <a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a> <a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not r\">C21</a> <a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33</a> <a href=\"#c34\" title=\"3 May 1988 · Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.\">C34</a> <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt. BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press; the family are publicly framed as \">C35</a> <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36</a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from\">C38</a> <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"lyr\" id=\"layer-9\"><span class=\"mini\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:44px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:40px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:36px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:32px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:28px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:24px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:20px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:16px\"></i><i class=\"on\" style=\"width:12px\"></i></span><b>Layer 9 of 9: 1988: the fall</b><span class=\"muted\">Built on layers 1 to 8 and the peak.</span></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c33\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C33</span><span class=\"dt\">1987–88</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (petition); outcome papers not yet held</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The last domestic route closed.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0076-house-of-lords-petition-leave-papers/\">EV-0076</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c34\" title=\"3 May 1988 · Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.\">C34</a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from\">C38</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c34\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C34</span><span class=\"dt\">3 May 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Application to the European Commission of Human Rights (14464/88), later declared inadmissible.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The international route closed without a hearing on the merits.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0122-echr-application-14464-88-inadmissibility/\">EV-0122</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a> <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c35\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C35</span><span class=\"dt\">Apr–May 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press); the label is others&#x27;, not ours</span></div><div class=\"ev\">First eviction attempt. BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press; the family are publicly framed as people with no right to be there.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> In public the family became occupiers resisting bailiffs, the &quot;squatters&quot; label others applied, rather than a family with an undecided ownership plea.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0089-chainsaw-farmer-vows-fight-on/\">EV-0089</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0090-south-wales-echo-bailiffs-medical-attention/\">EV-0090</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0088-south-wales-echo-buckler-dispute-1988/\">EV-0088</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0092-echo-alun-michael-lord-chancellor/\">EV-0092</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c37\" title=\"29 Jul – Dec 1988 · Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.\">C37</a> <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from\">C38</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c36\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C36</span><span class=\"dt\">9 Jul 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press); our reading (motive)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> Our reading: the site was now an asset for sale, which gave a motive to clear it. Nothing yet ties the 1982–83 filings to this sale.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0093-estates-gazette-1988-bp-welsh-sales/\">EV-0093</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a> <a href=\"#c31\" title=\"2 Feb 1987 · The farmhouse title is merged into the farm title (application, WA231076 item 14) while the appeal is pendi\">C31</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c37\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C37</span><span class=\"dt\">29 Jul – Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The heritage protection that might have saved the house came too late to stop the demolition.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0094-cadw-barn-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0094</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0095-cadw-farmhouse-survey-photo-1988/\">EV-0095</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0096-cadw-1988-inspection-photographs-listing/\">EV-0096</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0103-echo-history-fight-save-farm/\">EV-0103</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt. BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press; the family are publicly framed as \">C35</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c38\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C38</span><span class=\"dt\">30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital bed to face an assault charge.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The physical removal of the family. The charge put the son in the dock rather than BP.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0098-south-wales-echo-forced-entry-1988/\">EV-0098</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0099-south-wales-echo-bp-summons-1988/\">EV-0099</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0101-echo-extract-hospital-assault-charges/\">EV-0101</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0102-billys-unhappy-family-echo-1988/\">EV-0102</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a> <a href=\"#c33\" title=\"1987–88 · Petition for leave to appeal to the House of Lords.\">C33</a> <a href=\"#c35\" title=\"Apr–May 1988 · First eviction attempt. BP&#x27;s spokesman explains the case to the press; the family are publicly framed as \">C35</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c39\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C39</span><span class=\"dt\">6 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The last court door closed on the day before the demolition.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0104-south-wales-echo-extract-1988/\">EV-0104</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0105-western-mail-final-eviction-hearing-1988/\">EV-0105</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from\">C38</a> <a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a><br>Enabled: <a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40</a></div></div>\n<div class=\"cut\" id=\"c40\"><div class=\"hd\"><span class=\"cid\">C40</span><span class=\"dt\">7 Dec 1988</span><span class=\"lab l-rec\">Record (press, SMR)</span></div><div class=\"ev\">The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).</div><div class=\"blow\"><b>The blow:</b> The apex. With the house gone there was nothing left to occupy, list or restore. The Sites and Monuments Record later entered: &quot;building destroyed by owners&quot;.</div><div class=\"refs\">Evidence: <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0106-tears-flow-farmhouse-razed-1988/\">EV-0106</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0107-south-wales-echo-1988-councillor-protest/\">EV-0107</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0108-south-wales-echo-bp-demolition-anger/\">EV-0108</a></div><div class=\"deps\">Depends on: <a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39</a> <a href=\"#c37\" title=\"29 Jul – Dec 1988 · Cadw inspects and photographs the house; the listing decision comes in December 1988.\">C37</a> <a href=\"#c36\" title=\"9 Jul 1988 · Estates Gazette: &quot;BP signal Welsh sales&quot;.\">C36</a><br>Enabled: <em>the apex: nothing above it</em></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"spine\">The spine: one line from the peak to the fall</h2><p>Follow any cut's \"depends on\" links down and you reach the peak. This is the longest single chain, read from the base up:</p><ol class=\"spine\">\n<li><a href=\"#p1\" title=\"1870s–1916 · John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names h\">P1</a> 1870s–1916: John Williams holds Great House Farm from the Bute estate; a Feb 1916 Bute yearly tenancy with plan names him;…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c01\" title=\"Feb 1916 · Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.\">C01</a> Feb 1916: Bute grants John Williams a yearly agricultural tenancy of &quot;the whole of the farm&quot;, with plan.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c02\" title=\"23–25 Dec 1938 · Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance \">C02</a> 23–25 Dec 1938: Bute (Mountjoy) sells the reversion to Western Ground Rents Ltd, a ground-rent company; the conveyance later b…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c04\" title=\"mid-1930s and late 1940s · The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.\">C04</a> mid-1930s and late 1940s: The courts record John Williams as falling into rent arrears.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c05\" title=\"2 Feb 1949 · John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law F\">C05</a> 2 Feb 1949: John Williams&#x27;s tenancy is surrendered and a new yearly agricultural tenancy is granted to his son-in-law Fred…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c09\" title=\"2 Feb 1955 · A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.\">C09</a> 2 Feb 1955: A notice to quit ends Frederick Buckler&#x27;s tenancy.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c10\" title=\"1955 and 4 Jul 1955 · Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces \">C10</a> 1955 and 4 Jul 1955: Western Ground Rents obtains a summary possession order (Order 14) in the High Court and enforces it on 4 July…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c13\" title=\"11 Dec 1962 · Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne pr\">C13</a> 11 Dec 1962: Cardiff County Court possession order for the farmhouse and garden (Judge Temple Morris QC), with mesne profit…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c19\" title=\"17–19 Sep 1974 · BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforce\">C19</a> 17–19 Sep 1974: BP Pension Trust gets leave to execute the 1962 order (Judge Watkin Powell); the warrant may be enforced from …</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c20\" title=\"31 Oct 1974 · Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free f\">C20</a> 31 Oct 1974: Two letters, from BP Pension Trust and BP Properties, sent to her solicitor, allow her to stay rent-free for l…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c21\" title=\"Nov–Dec 1974 · On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not r\">C21</a> Nov–Dec 1974: On her solicitors&#x27; advice she does nothing while the 12 years from the 1962 order run out, and does not reject…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c25\" title=\"23 Feb 1983 · BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has \">C25</a> 23 Feb 1983: BP Properties applies to register the farmhouse (Form 1C, WA240304) while Mary is alive. A BP officer has to s…</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c26\" title=\"26 Mar 1983 · Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).\">C26</a> 26 Mar 1983: Mary Williams (Mrs Buckler) dies, after an illness in the weeks before (family testimony).</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c29\" title=\"May 1984 · BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.\">C29</a> May 1984: BP Properties issues a writ for possession against her son, the occupier.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c30\" title=\"10–24 Jul 1986 · High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.\">C30</a> 10–24 Jul 1986: High Court trial in Cardiff; Hollis J gives judgment for BP.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c32\" title=\"31 Jul 1987 · Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six wee\">C32</a> 31 Jul 1987: Court of Appeal: BP Properties Ltd v Buckler [1987] EWCA Civ 2 dismisses the appeal. Possession in six weeks; …</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c38\" title=\"30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988 · Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from\">C38</a> 30 Nov – 3 Dec 1988: Forced entry and the outbuilding roof removed; the residents are evicted; Mr Buckler is taken from a hospital …</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c39\" title=\"6 Dec 1988 · The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.\">C39</a> 6 Dec 1988: The final eviction hearing in the Cardiff High Court fails.</li>\n<li><a href=\"#c40\" title=\"7 Dec 1988 · The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).\">C40</a> 7 Dec 1988: The farmhouse is demolished (&quot;Tears flow as 800 year-old farm house is razed at last&quot;).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"after\">After the fall</h2><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>11 Feb 1989</b>: Vale councillors authorise legal action against BP Properties over the demolition. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0117-south-wales-echo-1989-vale-legal-action/\">EV-0117</a></li><li><b>Mar 1989</b>: Sites and Monuments Record PRN 02038s: &quot;building destroyed by owners&quot;. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0118-smr-record-card-1989-building-destroyed/\">EV-0118</a></li><li><b>13 Mar 1990</b>: Outline planning permission for houses at Great House Farm (89/01396/OUT). <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0124-outline-planning-permission-89-01396-out-residenti/\">EV-0124</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0114-planning-report-89-01396-out-outline-permission/\">EV-0114</a></li><li><b>1992–94</b>: Reserved matters approved and 20 houses built. <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0127-planning-application-form-d-for-approval-of-reserv/\">EV-0127</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0129-approved-planning-drawings-ref-92-00671-res-screen/\">EV-0129</a> <a href=\"/evidence/ev-0133-planning-drawings-ideal-homes-wales-llandough-farm/\">EV-0133</a></li></ul><p>No record found so far shows compensation to the family, or a finding of fault against anyone, for the demolition.</p>\n<h2 id=\"act-1983\">The 1983 Act</h2><p>Which 1983 Act: the Commons Registration (Glamorgan) Act 1983 (c. ix; Royal Assent 26 Jul 1983, in force 1 Sep 1983), EV-0232. It is the only 1983 statute our research has read and catalogued for the farm. Our reading is that it did not reach the farmhouse or VG41 directly, so it is listed as a cut with that counter-note. If the 1983 step meant is BP&#x27;s 1983 registration of the farmhouse, that is cuts C25 and C27.</p>\n<h2 id=\"reading\">Our reading: diminished, never extinguished</h2><div class=\"reading\"><p>Our reading: across 39 cuts from 1916 to 1988 the family&#x27;s standing was cut down piece by piece: first as tenants (1916, 1949), then as occupiers under a court order (1955, 1962), then as licensees by letter (1974), then as occupiers of land registered to someone else (1983), and finally as people removed by force (1988).</p><p>None of these steps decided who owned the house. The 1974 ownership plea was adjourned part-heard and &quot;has never been finally heard&quot;. The 1986 and 1987 courts decided possession and limitation, not the family&#x27;s ownership plea.</p><p>So, on our reading, the family&#x27;s rights were diminished step by step, but their ownership claim was never tested on its merits and never extinguished by any decision on it.</p><p>The outcome was eviction, demolition, no compensation and no finding against anyone. Presenting that as settled and fair rests on these cuts, not on a decision about ownership. That is the moral point of this page, and we put it as our reading, not as a finding.</p></div>\n<h3>What would confirm it</h3><ul class=\"tight\"><li>The 1974 Cardiff County Court file, including the part-heard action and the leave application (HMCTS reply due 2 Nov 2026), would show what was pleaded and what was never decided.</li><li>The Land Registry&#x27;s 1983 application papers and the 8 Apr, 12 Apr and 12 May 1983 letters (subject access request due 28 Oct 2026) would show what BP told the Registry about who lived in the house.</li><li>A letter from Mary or her solicitors after 31 Oct 1974 rejecting the licence would meet the exact point the Court of Appeal said might have changed the result.</li><li>The 1938 Bute–Western Ground Rents conveyance and plan would show whether the farmhouse parcel was ever in the paper chain.</li></ul>\n<h3>What cuts against it</h3><ul class=\"tight\"><li>The courts found the opposite on the points they decided. The Court of Appeal held that the 1962 order stopped the clock before 12 years had run, and that from the 1974 letters her possession was no longer adverse. Both points bind unless a ground to reopen is made out.</li><li>The judgment records rent arrears in the 1930s and 1940s and a last payment in 1953. That is against the family&#x27;s 1928 account.</li><li>The Court of Appeal did accept that Frederick and Mary were in adverse possession from 1955. The loss came from the order and the letters, not from any finding that the family never possessed as owners.</li><li>BP did not need the 1983 registration to sue. It sued in May 1984 and won on the 1974 letters.</li><li>No record yet shows BP knew of Mary&#x27;s final illness, or that the 1983 filing was timed to it.</li><li>Several peak items (Marconi&#x27;s stay, Driscoll&#x27;s fight, the 1928 receipt) are family testimony or not yet confirmed.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"muted\">Version 1.0.0, 2026-10-25. Sources: the Court of Appeal judgment (EV-0080), the evidence pages linked above, and the 1983 forensic chronology. Each cut is one row in the catalogue, with its links and dependencies. <a href=\"#tc-top\">Back to top</a></p>\n</div>"}};
